  "honest_limits": [
    "The positional block is `bins * 4**min(k,2)` = 96 features, NOT bins * 4**k. The clamp lives inside `positional_features` rather than at the call site, so `both` is 352 features and not 1792. Every p-against-n reading here depends on that.",
    "Ten seeds per cell. Each comparison between cells is seed-PAIRED, which is what makes a difference of this size readable at n=10; the per-cell margins themselves are noisier.",
    "A higher-order Markov chain fitted on 600 windows of 150bp approaches memorising its training set, so a high-order null is not simply a 'better' null -- part of any change is overfitting the fit half rather than modelling the substrate. This sweep measures the effect and does NOT separate those two causes.",
    "One organism, one window length, one geometry. The cross-organism behaviour of these levers is not measured here.",
    "A winnable region is necessary, NOT sufficient: all three feature sets see LOCAL composition, so the positional block adds WHERE composition sits, not long-range organisation."
  ],
  "wall_seconds": 48.2,
  "note_on_the_committed_grid": "The committed grid scores modes kmer and both at order 3 only. The positional-alone column and every non-3 order here are NEW cells, not a re-reading of that grid."
